milar. Show-off maybe less severe? Not open to new ideas also a problem for adaptability.\n\nWe might consider overall balance: Candidate A has strong leadership and anticipation, which are crucial for long-distance flights. The negative traits are more about attitude but may be mitigated. Candidate D has strong technical and responsibility but hot temper could be dangerous under stress.\n\nI think Candidate A might be best overall, given strong operational reliability (leadership, anticipation) and technical competence (spatial vision). The show-off and not open to new ideas are concerns but perhaps less critical than communication hostility.\n\nThus I will recommend Candidate A.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: there is none, but we can say \"Given the current facts, I propose...\"\n\nPublic message: state recommendation, reference facts, explain.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate A.\n\nProceed."}
